  "language": "en",
  "text": "At March 1978, in rough seas off Molokai, the Voyaging canoe Hokula lies capsized. 16 crew members cling to its hull. One of them is about to make a choice Hawaii still remembers. Eddie A. Cow was Wami Abe's first lifeguard. He pulled more than 500 people from the ocean, not one person drowned on his watch. Now his own crew needed saving. Their voyage to Tahiti had lasted only hours. They were drifting cold and far from hell. So Eddie put on a life vest, grabbed his surfboard, and paddled toward Lennie to get rescuers. That night, a passing airliner spotted the crew's flares. Everyone on the canoe was rescued. Everyone except Eddie. Searchers covered the ocean by air and sea. His body was never found. He was 31. What happened to him out there? No one knows. But Hawaii remembers what he chose. Today, three words carry his legacy. Eddie Wood.",
  "segments": [
    {
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 5780,
      "text": "At March 1978, in rough seas off Molokai, the Voyaging canoe Hokula lies capsized."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 6000,
      "endMs": 8020,
      "text": "16 crew members cling to its hull."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 8360,
      "endMs": 11100,
      "text": "One of them is about to make a choice Hawaii still remembers."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 11460,
      "endMs": 14040,
      "text": "Eddie A. Cow was Wami Abe's first lifeguard."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 14280,
      "endMs": 18480,
      "text": "He pulled more than 500 people from the ocean, not one person drowned on his watch."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 18840,
      "endMs": 20340,
      "text": "Now his own crew needed saving."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 20640,
      "endMs": 22960,
      "text": "Their voyage to Tahiti had lasted only hours."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 23260,
      "endMs": 25340,
      "text": "They were drifting cold and far from hell."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 25340,
      "endMs": 30360,
      "text": "So Eddie put on a life vest, grabbed his surfboard, and paddled toward Lennie to get rescuers."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 30520,
      "endMs": 33260,
      "text": "That night, a passing airliner spotted the crew's flares."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 33560,
      "endMs": 34960,
      "text": "Everyone on the canoe was rescued."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 35240,
      "endMs": 36260,
      "text": "Everyone except Eddie."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 36500,
      "endMs": 38560,
      "text": "Searchers covered the ocean by air and sea."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 38940,
      "endMs": 40120,
      "text": "His body was never found."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 40400,
      "endMs": 40980,
      "text": "He was 31."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 41380,
      "endMs": 42500,
      "text": "What happened to him out there?"
    },
    {
      "startMs": 42740,
      "endMs": 43300,
      "text": "No one knows."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 43740,
      "endMs": 45280,
      "text": "But Hawaii remembers what he chose."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 45520,
      "endMs": 47720,
      "text": "Today, three words carry his legacy."
    },
    {
      "startMs": 47980,
      "endMs": 48480,
      "text": "Eddie Wood."
    }
  ],
